1
00:00:03,069 --> 00:00:05,380
Before that briefing can happen, a reporter

2
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:08,087
puts a different question to Jensen Huang.

3
00:00:08,137 --> 00:00:10,491
It’s about a woman inside Nvidia.

4
00:00:10,541 --> 00:00:12,432
Her name is Kimberly Powell.

5
00:00:12,482 --> 00:00:14,220
She joined the company in 2008,

6
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:16,380
when her job was to get Nvidia chips

7
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:18,431
into medical imaging equipment.

8
00:00:18,481 --> 00:00:20,005
By 2026,

9
00:00:20,055 --> 00:00:22,400
she runs the company’s healthcare business,

10
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:24,480
overseeing technology used in everything

11
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:27,095
from medical scans to drug discovery.

12
00:00:27,145 --> 00:00:29,156
She reports directly to Huang.

13
00:00:29,206 --> 00:00:31,560
On November eleventh, The New York Times reports

14
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:33,793
that Huang and Powell had an affair,

15
00:00:33,843 --> 00:00:36,449
citing five people who worked at Nvidia.

16
00:00:36,499 --> 00:00:39,071
When a reporter calls Huang to ask about Powell,

17
00:00:39,121 --> 00:00:40,820
he says, “I don’t think you should

18
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:42,358
be talking to me directly.”

19
00:00:42,408 --> 00:00:44,936
Then he hangs up, according to the Times.

20
00:00:44,986 --> 00:00:47,280
Powell and Nvidia don’t immediately respond

21
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:48,748
to requests for comment.

22
00:00:48,798 --> 00:00:51,100
Reuters says it couldn’t immediately verify

23
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:52,479
the Times report.

24
00:00:52,529 --> 00:00:54,688
Open Nvidia’s code of conduct.

25
00:00:54,738 --> 00:00:57,196
The first letter is signed by Jensen Huang.

26
00:00:57,246 --> 00:00:58,840
A few pages later, the company

27
00:00:58,890 --> 00:01:01,180
lists personal relationships among the things

28
00:01:01,230 --> 00:01:03,242
that can create a conflict of interest.

29
00:01:03,292 --> 00:01:04,960
If a conflict arises,

30
00:01:05,010 --> 00:01:07,360
the code says employees should remove themselves

31
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:09,093
from decisions on the matter.

32
00:01:09,143 --> 00:01:10,660
The Times report leaves a question

33
00:01:10,710 --> 00:01:11,818
for the company.

34
00:01:11,868 --> 00:01:13,180
Did the alleged relationship

35
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:15,689
affect any decisions inside Nvidia?

36
00:01:15,739 --> 00:01:17,526
That night, according to Reuters,

37
00:01:17,576 --> 00:01:20,668
Nvidia’s directors meet to consider removing Huang.

38
00:01:20,718 --> 00:01:21,900
Three days earlier,

39
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:23,720
the board had publicly expressed confidence

40
00:01:23,770 --> 00:01:25,630
in him and his leadership team.

41
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:27,820
Now the company he co-founded is preparing

42
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:29,489
for a change at the top.

43
00:01:29,539 --> 00:01:32,035
The date is in Nvidia’s securities filing.

44
00:01:32,085 --> 00:01:34,180
On November eleventh, the board accepts

45
00:01:34,230 --> 00:01:36,837
Huang’s resignation, effective immediately.

46
00:01:36,887 --> 00:01:39,895
On November twelfth, the company announces it.

47
00:01:39,945 --> 00:01:41,759
After thirty-three years,

48
00:01:41,809 --> 00:01:44,468
Jensen Huang is out as chief executive.

49
00:01:44,518 --> 00:01:45,780
He also resigns as president

50
00:01:45,830 --> 00:01:47,897
and gives up his seat on the board.

51
00:01:47,947 --> 00:01:51,206
Colette Kress, Nvidia’s finance chief since 2013,

52
00:01:51,256 --> 00:01:52,800
takes over as interim CEO.

53
00:01:52,850 --> 00:01:54,340
The directors begin looking

54
00:01:54,390 --> 00:01:55,852
for a permanent replacement,

55
00:01:55,902 --> 00:01:57,260
and they name longtime director

56
00:01:57,310 --> 00:01:59,956
Harvey Jones the company’s first board chair.

57
00:02:00,006 --> 00:02:01,580
Nvidia is five days away

58
00:02:01,630 --> 00:02:03,731
from reporting its quarterly results.

59
00:02:03,781 --> 00:02:06,371
Then, with the resignation already public,

60
00:02:06,421 --> 00:02:08,247
Reuters breaks another story.

61
00:02:08,297 --> 00:02:10,740
Two people familiar with the matter tell Reuters

62
00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:12,800
that Huang had an intimate relationship

63
00:02:12,850 --> 00:02:15,205
with another Nvidia employee.

64
00:02:15,255 --> 00:02:17,743
A different woman from Kimberly Powell.

65
00:02:17,793 --> 00:02:19,140
Reuters withholds her name

66
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:21,107
and says it couldn’t reach her.

67
00:02:21,157 --> 00:02:23,174
Nvidia declines to comment.

68
00:02:23,224 --> 00:02:25,000
Huang, Powell, and a representative

69
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:26,640
for the board don’t respond

70
00:02:26,690 --> 00:02:28,704
to Reuters’ requests for comment.

71
00:02:28,754 --> 00:02:30,800
In four days, Nvidia has gone

72
00:02:30,850 --> 00:02:33,713
from its founder’s email to a new chief executive

73
00:02:33,763 --> 00:02:36,995
and two reports involving women inside the company.

74
00:02:37,045 --> 00:02:39,100
Then a government statement from Singapore

75
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:41,511
puts the focus back on Alice Huang.

76
00:02:41,561 --> 00:02:44,240
By the time the public saw the intelligence allegations,

77
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:46,947
Singapore’s police had already taken her passport,

78
00:02:46,997 --> 00:02:49,370
given it back, and barred her from returning.

79
00:02:54,003 --> 00:02:56,506
On June twenty-fourth, 2025,

80
00:02:56,556 --> 00:02:58,397
Alice Huang is present when officials

81
00:02:58,447 --> 00:02:59,917
from the U.S. Commerce Department

82
00:02:59,967 --> 00:03:03,329
carry out a post-shipment check at Megaspeed.

83
00:03:03,379 --> 00:03:05,648
According to Singapore’s Home Affairs Ministry,

84
00:03:05,698 --> 00:03:07,377
that’s when Singapore first learns

85
00:03:07,427 --> 00:03:09,257
that American authorities are interested

86
00:03:09,307 --> 00:03:10,894
in her and the company.

87
00:03:10,944 --> 00:03:12,737
Singapore’s police and customs officers

88
00:03:12,787 --> 00:03:14,613
have already been investigating

89
00:03:14,663 --> 00:03:16,077
possible false declarations

90
00:03:16,127 --> 00:03:18,914
involving server purchases for four months.

91
00:03:18,964 --> 00:03:21,364
That same day, police question Alice.

92
00:03:21,414 --> 00:03:23,257
They take her passport so they can secure

93
00:03:23,307 --> 00:03:25,354
her attendance during the investigation.

94
00:03:25,404 --> 00:03:27,377
The servers in Singapore’s account have passed

95
00:03:27,427 --> 00:03:29,618
through the country on their way to Malaysia.

96
00:03:29,668 --> 00:03:31,437
Investigators are trying to find out

97
00:03:31,487 --> 00:03:32,497
whether they went farther

98
00:03:32,547 --> 00:03:34,305
than the paperwork said they would.

99
00:03:34,355 --> 00:03:36,985
To do that, they need records from overseas.

100
00:03:37,035 --> 00:03:39,281
One company they turn to is Supermicro,

101
00:03:39,331 --> 00:03:41,026
an American server supplier.

102
00:03:41,076 --> 00:03:42,777
Singapore says the company provided

103
00:03:42,827 --> 00:03:44,082
limited cooperation,

104
00:03:44,132 --> 00:03:46,237
and that repeated requests to U.S. authorities

105
00:03:46,287 --> 00:03:47,497
brought limited help

106
00:03:47,547 --> 00:03:49,342
in obtaining information about it.

107
00:03:49,392 --> 00:03:52,657
By February 2026, Singapore police and prosecutors

108
00:03:52,707 --> 00:03:55,417
say they have insufficient evidence to establish

109
00:03:55,467 --> 00:03:57,125
that Alice committed an offense

110
00:03:57,175 --> 00:03:59,543
tied to the suspected false declarations.

111
00:03:59,593 --> 00:04:01,137
Police also say they assessed

112
00:04:01,187 --> 00:04:03,197
that she knowingly gave them inaccurate

113
00:04:03,247 --> 00:04:06,004
information to downplay her role at Megaspeed.

114
00:04:06,054 --> 00:04:07,357
They issue a stern warning

115
00:04:07,407 --> 00:04:09,735
and bar her from re-entering Singapore.

116
00:04:09,785 --> 00:04:11,144
On February twenty-sixth,

117
00:04:11,194 --> 00:04:12,626
she gets her passport back.

118
00:04:12,676 --> 00:04:14,493
She leaves the country that day.

119
00:04:14,543 --> 00:04:16,417
Nine months later, Bloomberg reports

120
00:04:16,467 --> 00:04:18,377
that Alice is living in Beijing.

121
00:04:18,427 --> 00:04:19,723
When asked to confirm that,

122
00:04:19,773 --> 00:04:21,357
China’s Foreign Ministry spokesperson

123
00:04:21,407 --> 00:04:23,578
says she’s unfamiliar with it.

124
00:04:23,628 --> 00:04:26,244
Beijing has denied the spying allegation.

125
00:04:26,294 --> 00:04:27,986
There’s another development in China,

126
00:04:28,036 --> 00:04:29,416
and it starts with a shipment

127
00:04:29,466 --> 00:04:30,724
that’s waiting to move.

128
00:04:30,774 --> 00:04:32,597
In early November, Reuters reports

129
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:34,557
that about six hundred thousand

130
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:37,743
Nvidia H200 chips are sitting in Hong Kong.

131
00:04:37,793 --> 00:04:39,404
Chinese companies want them.

132
00:04:39,454 --> 00:04:41,057
Some H200s have already

133
00:04:41,107 --> 00:04:42,557
been allowed into mainland China.

134
00:04:42,607 --> 00:04:44,497
Beijing is holding back approval

135
00:04:44,547 --> 00:04:46,452
for imports on that scale.

136
00:04:46,502 --> 00:04:47,797
Reuters had also reported

137
00:04:47,847 --> 00:04:49,377
a separate Chinese directive

138
00:04:49,427 --> 00:04:52,037
requiring new state-funded data center projects

139
00:04:52,087 --> 00:04:54,535
to use domestically made AI chips.

140
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:56,102
A sale can clear Washington

141
00:04:56,152 --> 00:04:58,439
and still get held up on the Chinese side.

142
00:04:58,489 --> 00:05:00,995
And for a company that needs computing power now,

143
00:05:01,045 --> 00:05:03,655
there’s still the option of renting it overseas.

144
00:05:03,705 --> 00:05:06,477
Reuters reports that some Chinese AI companies

145
00:05:06,527 --> 00:05:09,219
are trying to secure more of that capacity,

146
00:05:09,269 --> 00:05:11,437
worried that Washington could tighten the rules

147
00:05:11,487 --> 00:05:13,160
on remote access too.

148
00:05:13,210 --> 00:05:14,497
Against that backdrop,

149
00:05:14,547 --> 00:05:16,937
The Information makes a much larger claim

150
00:05:16,987 --> 00:05:19,395
about chips physically entering China.

151
00:05:19,445 --> 00:05:21,562
It reports that when orders stalled,

152
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:23,357
Alice used her connections to Nvidia

153
00:05:23,407 --> 00:05:26,067
and its distributors to secure supply.

154
00:05:27,313 --> 00:05:29,495
Its sources say she helped move roughly

155
00:05:29,545 --> 00:05:32,525
two hundred and forty thousand chips into China,

156
00:05:32,575 --> 00:05:35,557
worth at least seven and a half billion dollars.

157
00:05:35,607 --> 00:05:36,957
Reuters says it couldn’t

158
00:05:37,007 --> 00:05:39,076
independently verify the account.

159
00:05:39,126 --> 00:05:41,537
Megaspeed denies illegally diverting chips

160
00:05:41,587 --> 00:05:44,110
and says it has hired a U.S. law firm

161
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:45,177
to inventory its GPUs

162
00:05:45,227 --> 00:05:47,633
and review its export compliance.

163
00:05:47,683 --> 00:05:49,797
On November thirteenth, Malaysia confirms

164
00:05:49,847 --> 00:05:52,090
that Megaspeed’s local subsidiary,

165
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:54,184
Speedmatrix, imported servers

166
00:05:54,234 --> 00:05:56,872
and AI chips as a data center tenant.

167
00:05:56,922 --> 00:05:58,884
Its trade ministry says it’s working

168
00:05:58,934 --> 00:06:00,017
with customs to establish

169
00:06:00,067 --> 00:06:02,754
whether any of those chips were exported again,

170
00:06:02,804 --> 00:06:04,117
and whether any such shipments

171
00:06:04,167 --> 00:06:06,025
complied with Malaysian law.

172
00:06:06,075 --> 00:06:09,172
That gives investigators a concrete place to look.

173
00:06:09,222 --> 00:06:12,020
They know which company brought the equipment in.

174
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:14,595
They’re checking what happened after it arrived.

175
00:06:14,645 --> 00:06:16,937
In Washington, Attorney General Todd Blanche

176
00:06:16,987 --> 00:06:19,505
confirms the FBI is investigating.

177
00:06:19,555 --> 00:06:21,677
He says the Justice Department has yet to reach

178
00:06:21,727 --> 00:06:23,627
a conclusion on whether Alice worked

179
00:06:23,677 --> 00:06:25,157
for Chinese intelligence.

180
00:06:25,207 --> 00:06:26,277
And the congressional briefing

181
00:06:26,327 --> 00:06:28,183
mentioned earlier has moved.

182
00:06:28,233 --> 00:06:30,561
The House chairs now want a closed-door,

183
00:06:30,611 --> 00:06:32,537
transcribed interview with Jensen Huang

184
00:06:32,587 --> 00:06:34,036
on December first.

185
00:06:34,086 --> 00:06:36,847
They want Nvidia’s top lawyer the following day.

186
00:06:36,897 --> 00:06:38,338
If Huang doesn’t accept,

187
00:06:38,388 --> 00:06:40,500
they say they’ll move to subpoena him.

188
00:06:40,550 --> 00:06:41,957
Nvidia can point to a filing

189
00:06:42,007 --> 00:06:44,811
and show exactly when its founder left.

190
00:06:44,861 --> 00:06:46,754
To answer what reached Beijing,

191
00:06:46,804 --> 00:06:49,583
investigators are still looking for the equivalent.

192
00:06:49,633 --> 00:06:52,704
A shipping record that shows where the hardware ended up.

193
00:06:52,754 --> 00:06:55,507
A customer record that shows who used it.

194
00:06:56,375 --> 00:06:58,977
And evidence of what, if anything, passed

195
00:06:59,027 --> 00:07:01,507
between Alice Huang and Chinese intelligence.

